OL,3,GNEWSAMeet the guardians who look after
OL,4,Athe island defibs
OL,5,
OL,6,FSt Agnes defibrillator guardian Grace
OL,7,FWindridge-Hicks, 35, who also
OL,8,Fvolunteers for the island's ambulance
OL,9,Fservice, said the device was located at
OL,10,Fthe centre of the island, on top of a
OL,11,Fbin.
OL,13,FTara McEvoy-Wilding looks after the
OL,14,Fdefibrillator on Lundy which she said
OL,15,Fwas a "true reflection" as the island
OL,16,Fwas 12 miles from the closest point on
OL,17,Fthe mainland.
